#! /usr/bin/dh-exec
afirewall.conf etc/afirewall
# THE SAME FILE AGAIN, WHERE IT CANNOT BE EDITED. /etc/afirewall/afirewall.conf is a conffile and
# is meant to be changed - ansible composes a host's ruleset by enabling flags in it. That leaves
# nothing on the host stating what the defaults WERE, so a configuration manager that wants the
# end state to follow from what it just did has nothing to start from and can only accumulate.
#
# It is not "everything off": the defaults enable inbound.ssh and the outbound half a host needs to
# be administered, resolve, and update. A restore that guessed at that would close ssh.
afirewall.conf usr/share/afirewall
afirewall/afirewall.py => /usr/sbin/afirewall
# TEMPLATES AND LISTS ARE THE PACKAGE'S, NOT THE ADMIN'S, so they ship here and are replaced on
# upgrade without a question. They used to install under /etc, which made debhelper mark all 73 of
# them conffiles - and an upgrade then kept an edited one, leaving an old template beside a new
# base.rules. That is exactly the three-way skew the package's own tests forbid, on the one machine
# where nothing is checking, and what it produces is a table nft refuses: a whole address family
# lost rather than one service.
#
# An override still works. afirewall reads /etc/afirewall first and falls back to here, so a
# changed ssh.rules under /etc wins - it just stops being the thing that decides what future
# upgrades may do.
lists usr/share/afirewall
templates usr/share/afirewall
# THE CATALOGUE, AND THE PACKAGE IS INERT WITHOUT IT. Since chapter 8 every service is a record in
# services.toml and base.rules loops over them, so a package that shipped the templates and not
# this one would render a firewall with no services at all - and would do it quietly, because an
# empty loop is not an error. It belongs beside templates and lists for the same reason they are
# there: it is the package's, revised as the package learns things, and an admin who needs a
# different record puts one in /etc/afirewall/services.toml, where it MERGES over this rather than
# replacing it.
services.toml usr/share/afirewall
